) to learn directly from text input has been a significant challenge in NLP.  One major problem is training ANNs that can handle complex situations and stay focused at the same time.  Most attempts so far have not been successful.  One major issue is that most successful models need to use complex data structures and external knowledge that are not directly related to the text input.  Our study shows that a simpler, more direct approach can be effective.  We developed a basic type of network that can learn directly from text input and still perform well.  Our network does not need any extra data or complex modules, and it can handle abstract reasoning and other complex tasks.  Our results show that this approach can learn directly from text input and still perform well.  These results encourage further research into simple, more direct approaches to this complex problem.  Our code can be found at a website called: https://github.com/harvard-nlp/TextEmbeddingBasedNNs.  We also released a dataset to help others with their own experiments.  The details can be found at: https://github.com/harvard-nlp/TextEmbeddingBasedNNs.  You can also visit that website to access the code and data. 
Abstract:  This study explores the challenge of training artificial neural networks (ANNs) to process natural language inputs directly.  In this research, we focus on a specific type of network called transformer-based networks, which are a type of machine learning architecture.  These networks are able to learn directly from text input and can even be simplified further by eliminating external knowledge sources.  Our study shows that a basic version of this network performs similarly well to more complex ones.  These networks are also able to handle complex tasks such as understanding relationships between words and can generalize to new situations.  Our study provides detailed information on how these networks can be applied to other tasks as well.  These networks are also shown to be more efficient in terms of data usage compared to other models.  Our study provides a comprehensive overview of this approach and highlights its potential benefits.  Our study also includes a list of all the code and data used in these experiments.  You can find the code and data online at: https://github.com/harvard-nlp/TextEmbeddingBasedNNs.  You can also access the code and data through this website. 
